The storage key was changed from `'orange-quality-checker-storage'` to `'leaf-disease-checker-storage'` in commit 5888756, causing users to lose persisted data (settings, history, favorites) on app update.

## Changes

- **Storage wrapper with lazy migration**: Wraps AsyncStorage to run migration before any operation (getItem/setItem/removeItem)
- **Memoized migration**: Single execution per session via promise caching; resets on failure for automatic retry
- **Cleanup logic**: Removes old key after checking for data, regardless of whether migration occurred
- **Graceful degradation**: Errors logged but not thrown; app continues with empty state if migration fails

## Implementation

```typescript
async function migrateStorage(): Promise<void> {
  if (migrationPromise) return migrationPromise;

  migrationPromise = (async () => {
    const oldData = await AsyncStorage.getItem(OLD_STORAGE_KEY);
    if (oldData) {
      const newData = await AsyncStorage.getItem(NEW_STORAGE_KEY);
      if (!newData) {
        await AsyncStorage.setItem(NEW_STORAGE_KEY, oldData);
      }
      await AsyncStorage.removeItem(OLD_STORAGE_KEY);
    }
  })().catch(() => migrationPromise = null);
}

const storageWithMigration = {
  getItem: async (name) => {
    await migrateStorage();
    return AsyncStorage.getItem(name);
  },
  // ... setItem, removeItem
};
```

Zustand's persist middleware now uses `storageWithMigration` instead of raw AsyncStorage.

