Fix critical refresh issues when switching users - Dashboard, AgentBookingsPage, and SearchBookPage retain previous user's data.

## Issues to Fix:

### 1. CRITICAL: Dashboard shows previous user's data after logout/login

**Problem:** DashboardPage.refreshData() only called once in constructor. When User A logs out and User B logs in, dashboard still shows User A's statistics.

**Root cause:** No mechanism to refresh when user changes.

### 2. CRITICAL: AgentBookingsPage shows previous user's bookings

**Problem:** AgentBookingsPage.refreshTable() only called once in constructor. When switching users, User B sees User A's bookings.

### 3. MEDIUM: SearchBookPage retains previous user's filters

**Problem:** Search filters (from/to airports, date, airline, price) not cleared when user logs out. User B sees User A's search criteria.

## Solution:

### Step 1: Add signals to AccountManager

**Update include/core/AccountManager.h:**

Add signals section:
```cpp
#include <QObject>

class AccountManager : public QObject {
    Q_OBJECT

public:
    // ... existing methods ...

signals:
    void userLoggedIn(Account* user);
    void userLoggedOut();

private:
    // ... existing members ...
};
```

**Update src/core/AccountManager.cpp:**

Emit signals in login/logout methods:
```cpp
bool AccountManager::login(const std::string& username, const std::string& password) {
    // ... existing login logic ...

    if (loginSuccessful) {
        currentUser_ = user;
        emit userLoggedIn(currentUser_);  // Emit signal
        return true;
    }
    return false;
}

void AccountManager::logout() {
    currentUser_ = nullptr;
    emit userLoggedOut();  // Emit signal
}
```

### Step 2: Add refreshPage() method to DashboardPage

**Update src/UI/DashboardPage.h:**

```cpp
public slots:
    void refreshPage();  // New method to refresh when page shown or user changed
```

**Update src/UI/DashboardPage.cpp:**

```cpp
void DashboardPage::refreshPage() {
    // Call existing refreshData() to reload stats
    refreshData();
}
```

### Step 3: Add refreshPage() method to AgentBookingsPage

**Update src/UI/AgentBookingsPage.h:**

```cpp
public slots:
    void refreshPage();  // New method to refresh when page shown or user changed
```

**Update src/UI/AgentBookingsPage.cpp:**

```cpp
void AgentBookingsPage::refreshPage() {
    // Clear search fields
    bookingIdSearchEdit_->clear();
    fromSearchCombo_->setCurrentIndex(0);
    toSearchCombo_->setCurrentIndex(0);
    dateSearchEdit_->setDate(QDate::currentDate());

    // Reload table with current user's bookings
    refreshTable();
}
```

### Step 4: Add refreshPage() method to SearchBookPage

**Update src/UI/SearchBookPage.h:**

```cpp
public slots:
    void refreshPage();  // New method to clear filters and results
```

**Update src/UI/SearchBookPage.cpp:**

```cpp
void SearchBookPage::refreshPage() {
    // Clear all search filters
    fromSearchCombo_->setCurrentIndex(0);
    toSearchCombo_->setCurrentIndex(0);
    dateSearchEdit_->clear();
    airlineFilterCombo_->setCurrentIndex(0);
    priceMinEdit_->clear();
    priceMaxEdit_->clear();

    // Clear search results
    model_->removeRows(0, model_->rowCount());

    // Clear status label
    statusLabel_->setText("");
}
```

### Step 5: Connect signals in Application or MainWindow

**In the main application class (Application.cpp or MainWindow.cpp):**

Find where pages are created and add connections:

```cpp
// In constructor after creating pages

// Connect AccountManager signals to refresh all pages
connect(accountManager_, &AccountManager::userLoggedIn, 
        this, &Application::onUserChanged);
connect(accountManager_, &AccountManager::userLoggedOut, 
        this, &Application::onUserChanged);

// Also refresh current page when switching
connect(stackedWidget_, &QStackedWidget::currentChanged,
        this, &Application::onPageChanged);
```

**Add handler methods:**

```cpp
void Application::onUserChanged() {
    // Refresh all pages when user changes
    if (dashboardPage_) {
        dashboardPage_->refreshPage();
    }
    if (agentBookingsPage_) {
        agentBookingsPage_->refreshPage();
    }
    if (searchBookPage_) {
        searchBookPage_->refreshPage();
    }
}

void Application::onPageChanged(int index) {
    // Get current page and refresh it
    QWidget* currentPage = stackedWidget_->widget(index);

    if (DashboardPage* dashboard = qobject_cast<DashboardPage*>(currentPage)) {
        dashboard->refreshPage();
    } else if (AgentBookingsPage* bookings = qobject_cast<AgentBookingsPage*>(currentPage)) {
        bookings->refreshPage();
    } else if (SearchBookPage* search = qobject_cast<SearchBookPage*>(currentPage)) {
        search->refreshPage();
    }
}
```

